CodeBrix patch 0008 - surface capability usages: to_native_texture_usage_flags (wgpu-native/src/conv.rs)

WHAT: wgt::TextureUsages -> WGPUTextureUsage, which feeds WGPUSurfaceCapabilities.usages
(wgpuSurfaceGetCapabilities): COPY_DST now maps to WGPUTextureUsage_CopyDst (it mapped to
CopySrc - a copy-paste slip), and STORAGE_BINDING -> StorageBinding and TRANSIENT ->
TransientAttachment are no longer dropped.
WHY: a host deciding whether it may copy into, or write storage to, a swapchain texture read the
wrong answer.
UPSTREAM: backport of the to_native_texture_usage_flags hunk of commit
9b52924948ddfb9a0c23642099072debbd179264 ("Pull relevant changes from wgpu-native-complete",
Inner-Daemons, 2026-07-28), part of open PR gfx-rs/wgpu-native #630 (head 8322fe1a94). Adapted to
wgpu-types 29: the transient flag is TextureUsages::TRANSIENT there (TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT in
wgpu 30); the same hunk's STORAGE_ATOMIC raw-bit passthrough is NOT carried (no webgpu.h bit;
PR #630 reworks it again later). Trunk (589e6caa4e) still has the bug.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/conv.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/conv.rs
@@ -1831,14 +1831,20 @@ pub fn to_native_texture_usage_flags(flags: wgt::TextureUsages) -> native::WGPUT
         flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_CopySrc;
     }
     if flags.contains(wgt::TextureUsages::COPY_DST) {
-        flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_CopySrc;
+        flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_CopyDst;
     }
     if flags.contains(wgt::TextureUsages::TEXTURE_BINDING) {
         flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_TextureBinding;
     }
+    if flags.contains(wgt::TextureUsages::STORAGE_BINDING) {
+        flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_StorageBinding;
+    }
     if flags.contains(wgt::TextureUsages::RENDER_ATTACHMENT) {
         flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_RenderAttachment;
     }
+    if flags.contains(wgt::TextureUsages::TRANSIENT) {
+        flag |= native::WGPUTextureUsage_TransientAttachment;
+    }
     flag
 }
 
